      "Chapter 10 — Compare the Seven Side Hustles",
      "Side-by-side decision table\n| Side hustle | Starting cost | Time to first potential income | Main skill | Main risk |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| AI evaluation | Low | Depends on approval and project availability | Subject expertise and careful judgement | Eligibility and inconsistent tasks |\n| Live selling | Low if using owned items; higher with inventory | Potentially short after setup | Selling and product knowledge | Inventory and fulfilment |\n| UGC | Low if you own a phone | Depends on portfolio and client acquisition | Filming, scripting, editing | Finding paying clients and rights terms |\n| Ecommerce testing | Variable; can become capital-intensive | Depends on product and traffic test | Product research and unit economics | Losing money on stock or ads |\n| AI app | Low-cost prototype possible | Usually uncertain and not immediate | Problem-solving and product development | No users or poor retention |\n| Newsletter | Low | Usually slow | Research, writing, consistency | Slow audience growth |\n| Personal brand | Low | Usually slow | Communication and consistency | Long time to monetisation |",
      "The “time to first potential income” column is qualitative. It is not a promise. Even a low-cost model may take time to generate a paid opportunity.",
      "Which should you choose?\nChoose AI evaluation if: you have strong subject knowledge and meet platform eligibility requirements.",
      "Choose live selling if: you understand a product category, can source legitimate items, and are comfortable presenting live.",
      "Choose UGC if: you can create good short videos and are willing to pitch brands.",
      "Choose ecommerce testing if: you have some risk capital, can validate suppliers, and understand the costs of fulfilment.",
      "Choose an AI app if: you can identify a problem, build a reliable prototype, and reach potential users.",
      "Choose a newsletter if: you enjoy research and can serve a specific group consistently.",
      "Choose a personal brand if: you want a long-term distribution asset and can commit to a clear topic.",
      "Weighted student fit scorecard\nScore each model from 1 to 5. A high score means it fits your current situation.\n| Factor | AI evaluation | Live selling | UGC | Ecommerce | AI app | Newsletter | Personal brand |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Fits my weekly schedule |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Fits my available budget |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Uses skills I already have |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| I can reach the right people |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| I can start with a small test |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| I can sustain it for 90 days |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Total |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |",
      "Do not treat the highest score as an automatic answer. Use the table to identify which model deserves a small experiment."
